    "bands": [
      {
        "id": "identity-band",
        "kind": "identity",
        "step": "governance",
        "text": "Identity: the Fabric data agent tool passes the signed-in user's identity (on-behalf-of); service principals are not supported for this tool. Fabric permissions and row-level security decide what the agent sees."
      },
      {
        "id": "network-band",
        "kind": "network",
        "step": "external",
        "text": "Boundary: web grounding queries leave the Azure compliance and geo boundary and follow Bing's terms. Restrict domains, keep confidential data out of queries, and show citations."
      },
      {
        "id": "policy-band",
        "kind": "policy",
        "step": "governance",
        "text": "Authority: the data agent is read-only. Agents propose data fixes; a data steward approves; a Fabric pipeline corrects Silver upstream, never the report."
      },
      {
        "id": "evidence-band",
        "kind": "evidence",
        "step": "governance",
        "text": "Evidence: every run is traced and evaluated; brief numbers reconcile with the governed baseline (synthetic demonstration data)."
      }
    ],
    "columns": 7,
    "cue": "Build it left to right. Fabric owns the data and its meaning. Foundry owns reasoning, tools and orchestration. External web data enters only through a grounding tool you allow-list. Authority stays with Entra identity, guardrails and a human approval. Evidence comes from tracing and evaluations.",
